  "question": {
    "text": "Heat treatment of muscular pain involves radiation of wavelength of about $900 \\mathrm{nm}$. Which spectral line of $\\mathrm{H}$ atom is suitable for this purpose? $\\left[\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{H}}=1 \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1} \\cdot \\mathrm{h}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}, \\mathrm{c}=3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\right]$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Paschen, $\\infty \\rightarrow 3$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Paschen, $5 \\rightarrow 3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Balmer, $\\infty \\rightarrow 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Lyman, $\\infty \\rightarrow 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\lambda}=\\mathrm{R}\\left(\\frac{1}{n_{1}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{n_{2}^{2}}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$n_{1}=3, n_{2}=\\infty$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{1}{\\lambda}=\\mathrm{R}\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{9}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{9}{10^{5}}=9 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~cm}=900 \\mathrm{nm}$"
  }
}